// test-error
// ADR-022 forbids a ternary inside a ternary. TWO mechanisms enforce that, and
// this fixture holds the half that is NOT E0710.
//
// Unparenthesized, the nesting is a GRAMMAR error -- the parser rejects it and
// no analyzer ever runs. Parenthesized, it parses fine and E0710 rejects it in
// pass 2.1 (`nested-ternary-error` beside this file).
//
// #1322 moved it here from `tests/ternary/`, where its name suggested it
// covered ADR-022's rule. It covers the grammar. The audit that classified the
// codegen throws recorded "fixture: none" for the nested-ternary throw and was
// right: this fixture never reaches it.

void test() {
    i32 x <- 5;
    i32 sign <- (x > 0) ? 1 : (x < 0) ? -1 : 0;
}
